= Introduction

In this analysis, we measure coherent and incoherent $phi.alt$ meson photoproduction in ultra-peripheral Au+Au collisions (UPCs) at STAR.
The $phi.alt$ mesons are reconstructed through the charged-kaon decay channel, $phi.alt -> K^+ K^-$.
The primary goal of the analysis is to extract the differential production cross sections for the coherent and incoherent components.

@sec:dataset describes the dataset, trigger, and luminosity, and @sec:event_selection the event selection.
@sec:tracks establishes the track-quality requirement and the kaon identification, and @sec:candidates the coherent and incoherent candidate selections and their raw yields.
@sec:efficiencies presents the vertex and BBC-veto efficiencies.
Track distributions of the selected candidates are collected in @sec:app_tracks.
